{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q419209","formula":"C₁₀H₁₆N₂O₄","hill":"C10H16N2O4","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":16.0,"N":2.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Tetraacetylethylenediamine","uk":"Тетраацетилетилендіамін"},"descriptions":{"en":"Tetraacetylethylenediamine, commonly abbreviated as TAED, is an organic compound with the formula (CH3C(O))2NCH2CH2N(C(O)CH3)2. It is a white solid commonly used as a bleach activator in laundry detergents and in the production of paper pulp. TAED is synthesized through the acetylation of ethylenediamine.","uk":"Тетра́ацетилетиле́ндіамі́́н (Tetraacetylethylenediamine, зазвичай скорочено TAED) — органічна сполука з формулою (CH3C(O))2NCH2CH2N(C(O)CH3)2. Ця біла тверда речовина зазвичай використовується як активатор відбілювача в пральних порошках і для паперової маси. Він виробляється ацетилюванням етилендіаміну."},"fame":15,"pubchemCid":66347,"mass":228.24,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(=O)N(CCN(C(=O)C)C(=O)C)C(=O)C","inchikey":"BGRWYDHXPHLNKA-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"N-acetyl-N-[2-(diacetylamino)ethyl]acetamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"66347","atoms":32,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.026,"y":2.38,"z":0.221,"el":"O"},{"x":3.464,"y":-1.389,"z":-0.688,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.986,"y":2.379,"z":-0.221,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.496,"y":-1.396,"z":0.67,"el":"O"},{"x":1.85,"y":0.04,"z":0.263,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.839,"y":0.037,"z":-0.256,"el":"N"},{"x":0.434,"y":0.034,"z":0.64,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.444,"y":0.034,"z":-0.603,"el":"C"},{"x":2.54,"y":1.266,"z":0.082,"el":"C"},{"x":2.522,"y":-1.194,"z":0.083,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.529,"y":1.278,"z":-0.085,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.538,"y":-1.199,"z":-0.08,"el":"C"},{"x":3.993,"y":1.181,"z":-0.312,"el":"C"},{"x":2.049,"y":-2.342,"z":0.949,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.99,"y":1.231,"z":0.288,"el":"C"},{"x